# HW-019 - ES8311 sample-rate sweep + route transitions: PASS
# 2026-07-12, M5StickS3 on COM35 (ESP32-S3-PICO-1-N8R8, MAC 98:88:e0:0e:dc:64).
# A THIRD physical device, independent of the boards used for HW-006/HW-016 (COM9)
# and HW-018 (COM5). Image built from c6c6256 + the local i2s_esp32 fix below.
#
# RESULT: all 9 rates PASS, all 3 route transitions PASS, restore measured.
#
#   * Every rate 8 kHz - 48 kHz: the identical clock-register set reads back off the
#     chip (regs=OK), the frame clock is MEASURED against the kernel cycle counter
#     and lands within 5 Hz of target, and the ADC is alive with the amp off.
#     The 256fs argument (MCLK from BCLK, so one register set serves every rate) is
#     now hardware-verified end to end, not just argued from the datasheet.
#
#   * 8 kHz WORKS (measured 7999 Hz, ADC alive). Both Espressif reference drivers
#     special-case 8 kHz (x4 instead of x8) claiming BCLK must be >= 512 kHz. On this
#     silicon that special case is NOT needed. `8000` stays in es8311_rates[].
#
#   * The three route transitions read back 0x01/0x09/0x0A/0x0D/0x0E/0x12/0x14 exactly
#     as the driver intends, on the real part. Before this run those values had only
#     ever been checked against an emulator that cannot disagree with them.
#
#   * The sweep restores 16 kHz and MEASURES it (16000 Hz) before handing the device
#     back, so a sweep that killed audio could not report success.
#
# THIS RUN REQUIRED A FIX TO THE ZEPHYR ESP32 I2S DRIVER (not to the codec).
#
# drivers/i2s/i2s_esp32.c leaks one mem-slab block per direction on every
# START/DROP cycle: i2s_esp32_{rx,tx}_stop_transfer() NULLs stream->data->mem_block
# -- the block the DMA is working on -- without returning it to the slab. And
# i2s_buf_write() allocates with K_FOREVER (drivers/i2s/i2s_common.c), so an
# exhausted slab is not an error, it is an unkillable block.
#
# Measured on this board, BLOCK_COUNT = 8, one reconfigure per rate:
#
#     slab free (tx/rx)   8  7  6  5  4  3  2  1  -> i2s_buf_write() hangs forever
#     rate                8k 11k 12k 16k 22k 24k 32k 44.1k
#
# The sweep died silently at 44.1 kHz with no error and no fault, because a call that
# never returns prints nothing. With the fix the census reads 8/8 at every rate and
# the sweep completes. That is the run below.
#
# The fix (3 hunks, drivers/i2s/i2s_esp32.c):
#   1. i2s_esp32_tx_callback(): NULL mem_block after freeing it. The RX callback
#      already does; without this, part 2 is a double free on the tx_disable path.
#   2/3. i2s_esp32_{rx,tx}_stop_transfer(): free the in-flight block before dropping
#      the pointer.
#
# This is NOT specific to this board. It hits any ESP32 application that changes I2S
# sample rate, or stops and restarts a stream, more than BLOCK_COUNT times -- which
# includes this project's own audio app: entering and leaving the AUDIO page 8 times
# exhausts the slab and the 9th capture hangs. To be reported upstream.
#
